WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.050
What’s the largest animal you can think
of?

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:08.060
Okay, that’s probably too vague of a question,
your mind probably went straight to the oceans,

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.129
picturing deep sea leviathans like the mighty
Blue Whale.

00:00:11.129 --> 00:00:14.070
Let’s go a little bit closer, shall we?

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.830
What about on land, what’re the biggest
animals that live up here with us, above the

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:19.830
water?

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:20.830
Elephants, maybe?

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:21.830
What about rhinos?

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:27.100
Then again, hippos are up there too, in the
same kind of ballpark, all pretty huge.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.840
What about cows, they can grow to be pretty
big, right?

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.059
Especially with all the crazy growth hormones
that meat manufacturers pump into them these

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:35.059
days.

00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:38.980
Well, what if there was something out there
bigger than all of those?

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:44.489
Imagine it, some huge beast roaming the wilderness
that easily towered above any creature you’ve

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:46.379
ever seen in your life.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:51.839
This thing would be massive, striding across
the world, towering above the meager height

00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:53.559
of a human being.

00:00:53.559 --> 00:01:00.289
Now, imagine that this… thing, whatever
it was, wasn’t just big, but kept getting

00:01:00.289 --> 00:01:01.289
bigger.

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:06.390
Sure, all of this might sound like the premise
for the next Godzilla or Cloverfield movie,

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:11.729
but while Big Charlie might not be king of
the monsters, it certainly lives up to that

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:14.240
first part of its nickname.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:20.670
Of course, the SCP Foundation calls it SCP-4158;
“Big Charlie” is just the playful nickname

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:25.070
that the owners gave it, although none of
them are sure who was the first to call the

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.920
creature by that name.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:33.880
Standing on four long legs at 3.4 meters tall
when the Foundation first discovered it, SCP-4158

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:38.869
was about one-and-three-fifths times as tall
as famous professional basketball player Shaquille

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:39.869
O’Neal.

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:45.570
But since then, well, like we said, Big Charlie
is getting bigger day by day.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:50.039
The creature appears to be tangentially related
to the bovine family of mammals, essentially

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:52.929
making it a ginormous cow.

00:01:52.929 --> 00:01:57.780
However, SCP-4158 lacks the facial structure
and features that you might expect to see

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.479
on the faces at your local farm.

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:05.520
The creature has thin, translucent skin, which
is so fragile that it often tears easily,

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:11.670
and anyone observing SCP-4158 can often see
the bones and internal organs within.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:12.680
Gross.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:17.849
It possesses a large, bulbous head with a
protrusion at the front, almost like a beak.

00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:23.040
As well as that, its huge eyes are foggy,
a milky white color which seems to suggest

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.909
that SCP-4158 is, at least partially, blind.

00:02:27.909 --> 00:02:32.299
The large, cattle-like mammal is incredibly
skinny, almost to the point where its bones

00:02:32.299 --> 00:02:34.769
stick out from underneath its skin.

00:02:34.769 --> 00:02:40.550
Its legs are longer than the rest of its colossal
body and seem barely able to support the animal’s

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:41.550
weight.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:45.569
On description alone, you can’t help but
feel sorry for the poor creature and its sorry

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:46.849
state of living.

00:02:46.849 --> 00:02:51.489
Normally, Big Charlie is mostly calm and docile,
barely acknowledging the Foundation personnel

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:55.450
that come to examine it, feed it, or clean
its containment cell.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:01.040
Held in a heavy containment zone, SCP-4158
is fed through a five-meter trough on the

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:07.569
far east wall of its cell, surviving on a
diet of raw beef, hay, wood, and bricks.

00:03:07.569 --> 00:03:11.830
Not the typical “grass-only” eating habits
you’d expect from normal cows.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:15.720
But according to the Foundation’s extensive
testing on the creature, its diet doesn’t

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:21.090
seem to be what is causing SCP-4158 to keep
growing at the rate it has been.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:26.430
The mass of Big Charlie is in some sort of
state of perpetual increase, meaning its size

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.280
and weight are always growing.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:33.599
And it is because of this continuous growth
that every week the Foundation is forced to

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:39.519
shear off great swathes of excess meat from
the creature, cleaving off its flesh and incinerating

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:44.430
the mass, all while Big Charlie is still alive.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.760
Before you start dialing PETA’s hotline,
it’s also worth mentioning Big Charlie can’t

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.760
feel pain.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:55.540
What’s more, testing has revealed that the
meat taken from SCP-4158 is USDA Utility Grade

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.989
beef, the kind that would normally come from
older cattle.

00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:04.030
Utility Grade meat has no fat marbling, so
it isn’t as tender or as flavorsome as other

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:09.510
more premium grades, but would normally be
used in canned and processed food products.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:13.520
And, despite the Foundation destroying the
excess that they cut off of Big Charlie as

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:19.060
a precaution, in theory, the meat is still
good to eat and possesses no anomalous properties.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:26.650
Then again, would you really want to eat a
burger made from SCP-4158?

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:32.060
If left unchecked and allowed to grow for
longer than a week, SCP-4158 will begin to

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:37.960
form new features, limbs, organs and sometimes
even genitals will sprout from random places

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.590
all over its body.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:43.650
The previous record for Big Charlie’s most
substantial growth was when he increased to

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:48.340
eight and a half meters tall, that’s over
three-fifths the height of the Hollywood sign,

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:52.169
and over one-and-a-half times the average
height of a giraffe.

00:04:52.169 --> 00:04:57.070
At this immense size, Charlie had developed
seven legs, four stomachs, three tongues,

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:02.060
and numerous other extremities before the
SCP Foundation cut him back down to size.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:05.370
And we mean they literally cut him back down.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.230
So, what exactly is this thing?

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:13.520
It’s like a giant cow but not actually a
cow, even though its flesh is identical to

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:14.520
beef.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:19.490
And it’s not a destructive rampaging monster
either, showing no hostility towards humans

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.870
even when they are shearing its excess body
mass away.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:25.690
Could it be some kind of failed genetic experiment?

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:30.039
An attempt to solve hunger by engineering
a creature that can not only stay alive but

00:05:30.039 --> 00:05:32.410
keep growing after having its meat cut away?

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:38.400
If that were true, it would make SCP-4158
a literal cash cow for the meat industry.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.080
Well, we’ve got kind of a funny story about
that, actually…

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:49.030
Big Charlie was first encountered by the Foundation
back in December 2004, in Crewdson, Indiana.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:53.840
A number of calls had been made to the area’s
local animal control services, with reports

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:57.630
of a large cow with mange roaming the nearby
Highway 17.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:02.130
Two officers belonging to the animal control
department were sent out to investigate these

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:08.950
reports, and what they found was SCP-4158,
wandering aimlessly, but unlike any cow, they

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.569
had ever seen.

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:14.419
The officers called local police, where a
Foundation plant caught wind of what they

00:06:14.419 --> 00:06:17.509
had found and called in containment specialists.

00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:21.550
The case was closed after the animal control
officers were given amnestics, and a cover

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:26.380
story was put in place about a cow with mange
that was put down where it had been found.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:31.270
In reality, the SCP Foundation rounded up
old Big Charlie and transported it to safety

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.479
with little resistance from the animal.

00:06:33.479 --> 00:06:37.570
They were able to trace the creature’s origin
back to somewhere called Butcher’s Block,

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.669
a nearby slaughterhouse.

00:06:39.669 --> 00:06:45.199
The manager of the establishment, one Jeff
Fine, and a single employee named Barney Mossman,

00:06:45.199 --> 00:06:47.720
were brought in by the Foundation for questioning.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:52.740
Another employee, Rory Gildson, was also retrieved
from his home, after having called in sick

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:54.319
to work that day.

00:06:54.319 --> 00:06:57.740
Barney Mossman, the first of the Butcher’s
Block employees to be interviewed, stated

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:03.490
that SCP-4158 had been called “Big Charlie”
since long before he had started his job at

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.069
the slaughterhouse.

00:07:05.069 --> 00:07:08.980
According to his testimony, he knew nothing
about where the creature had actually come

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:14.580
from, only that it was fed hay but would also
occasionally eat anything else it could, including

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.110
other cows.

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:20.020
Since joining Butcher’s Block four years
earlier, Mossman had been told not to ask

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:23.039
questions or to tell anyone else about SCP-4158.

00:07:23.039 --> 00:07:29.669
The morning after the huge creature had seemingly
escaped, Mr. Fine had apparently angrily accused

00:07:29.669 --> 00:07:34.479
both Barney and Rory of selling him out and
giving Big Charlie away to the competitors

00:07:34.479 --> 00:07:38.970
of Butcher’s Block - even though they were
the only slaughterhouse in the area.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:42.629
But Mossman was convinced that neither of
them were capable of doing something like

00:07:42.629 --> 00:07:47.849
that, Rory apparently treated Big Charlie
like his own child, and Fine had an even stranger

00:07:47.849 --> 00:07:49.830
relationship with the creature.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:55.949
Rory Gildson, the other of Fine’s employees,
was more helpful in shedding light on SCP-4158’s

00:07:55.949 --> 00:07:57.849
origin than Barney had been.

00:07:57.849 --> 00:08:02.610
Rory explained that he and Jeff Fine had bought
a pregnant cow from an unknown person nine

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:07.520
years earlier, considering it to be a steal,
a two-for-the-price-of-one bargain.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.980
However, one day without warning, the calf
fell out of its mother.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:15.849
It wasn’t born like any ordinary cow however;
according to Gildson it had ripped through

00:08:15.849 --> 00:08:19.289
the mother cow’s chest, and looked disgusting.

00:08:19.289 --> 00:08:22.979
While Rory and Jeff had initially thought
the calf to be dead, they discovered it had

00:08:22.979 --> 00:08:26.699
tried to get back into the barn after they
had hauled it outside.

00:08:26.699 --> 00:08:30.819
Their original intention had been to sell
the creature off for scientific study or,

00:08:30.819 --> 00:08:32.820
failing that, to a freak show.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.970
However, after their attempts to sell the
calf failed, Jeff and Rory had decided the

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:40.360
best course of action would be to put the
animal down.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:44.900
They had reasoned that releasing it into the
wild could have negatively affected the ecosystem,

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:49.700
so instead, they took a bolt pistol and pushed
it between the creature’s eyes, then fired.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.370
But nothing happened.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:54.500
Rory tried again but ended up breaking the
gun instead.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:58.780
They slit the animal’s throat but it barely
bled, even butchering it there on the spot

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:01.140
while it was still alive did nothing.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:05.830
Fine and Gildson reduced the calf to little
more than a skeleton, but it simply refused

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:06.830
to die.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:10.370
The pair of them packaged the meat they had
removed with the rest, hoping no one would

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.670
notice or ask where it had come from.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:18.060
It was a few days later that Rory realized
SCP-4158 was capable of regrowing whatever

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.170
was cut off of it.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:23.070
He and his boss even tried some, and couldn’t
tell the difference.

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:26.730
They had their hands on a cow that would eat
anything put in front of it and that could

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:28.540
produce infinite meat.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:32.840
The Foundation probed Rory Gildson further
for more information on the creature, learning

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:39.510
that SCP-4158 was sterile and incapable of
reproducing, the only one of its kind.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:44.120
Rory argued that the Foundation legally couldn’t
take Big Charlie away, that the creature was

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.790
still private property.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.080
Little did he realize, he was wrong.

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:52.540
But he, just like Barney Mossman, also knew
nothing about how the animal had escaped in

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:53.950
the first place.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:58.030
Finally, Jeff Fine, the owner of the Butcher’s
Block slaughterhouse was questioned by the

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.030
Foundation.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:03.270
He repeated Rory’s earlier story about the
strange calf that had been born and how it

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:06.130
could regenerate the flesh that was sheared
off of it.

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:09.020
Fine remarked that he considered it to be
a blessing.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:14.140
When asked about his whereabouts on the night
SCP-4158 had escaped from Butcher’s Block,

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:16.630
Jeff admitted that he had been praying.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.820
But not to God, to Big Charlie.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:24.030
He had apparently been doing this every night
since realizing what the creature could do,

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:27.430
viewing the animal as a provider and a savior.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:30.030
“I just felt something when I was around
him.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:33.530
I could tell that he wanted to make this sacrifice
for us.

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:36.060
Ever since he tried to get into the barn after
we threw him out…

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:41.220
I knew he cared for us,” Fine told the Foundation,
“I would open his pen, take off my clothes

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:45.360
so that I was pure before him, lay down, and
receive his blessings.”

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.880
And how would he receive those blessings?

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.570
By drinking the animal’s blood.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:52.910
Yeah, Jeff Fine was a real eccentric like
that.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:57.850
One night, when Fine had entered the pen to
perform this weird ritual, Big Charlie had

00:10:57.850 --> 00:10:58.850
escaped.

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:02.800
But his owner was convinced that there must
have been a reason for this, that the animal

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.420
had some sort of goal.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:08.800
When the Foundation staff conducting Fine’s
interview dismissed this idea, the slaughterhouse

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.180
owner became enraged.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:12.670
“How dare you question Big Charlie!

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:15.181
He knows what’s best for all of us!

00:11:15.181 --> 00:11:16.181
I’m done here!

00:11:16.181 --> 00:11:18.820
I don’t need to keep answering questions
like this…

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:19.820
Let me out!

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:20.820
I need to see Big Charlie!

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.800
I need to see if he’s safe!”

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:28.100
The Foundation believes that Jeff Fine’s
practice of worshipping SCP-4158 was not due

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:31.380
to any anomalous effect caused by the creature
itself.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:36.420
None of the Foundation personnel tasked with
feeding, studying and shearing meat off of

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:41.750
Big Charlie have displayed any similar behavior
of performing abnormal religious rituals.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:45.300
He really was just a huge weirdo.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:49.250
As for the Butcher’s Block slaughterhouse,
Fine and the rest of his employees were given

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:55.140
amnestics to forget Big Charlie had ever even
existed, and the slaughterhouse was closed

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:59.830
under the false pretense of a health code
violation and its staff being arrested for

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.060
malpractice.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:05.600
The one question that remains unanswered,
however, is the identity of the individual

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:10.790
that first sold Jeff Fine the cow that gave
birth to SCP-4158.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:15.710
It just goes to show you though, sometimes
you don’t know where your food is coming

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:16.710
from.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:22.520
If you lived in Indiana in late 2004, who
knows – you might have eaten some of Big

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:25.970
Charlie and not even realized it.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:32.520
Now go check out “SCP-261 - Pan-Dimensional
Vending Machine” and “SCP-426 - I am a

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:35.790
Toaster” for more SCPs that might whet your
appetite!

